# Frozen implementation contract — admin announcements

Date 2026-10-18 · P2 · pending · 0%. This specifies future implementation, not deployed behavior. Authority: [decisions](02-design-decisions.md), [brainstorm](../../reports/brainstorm-261018-0228-server-admin-notifications.md). Research examples are superseded here. Changes require one coordinated contract amendment before consumers change; no independent endpoint guesses.

## 1. Identity, encoding, bounds and authority
- Hub application ID exactly `tabby-rush`; Android package `dev.tabbyrush.android`; Windows AUMID `dev.tabbyrush.desktop`.
- JSON camelCase, UTF-8; UTC RFC3339 timestamps with millisecond precision; IDs lowercase canonical UUIDv4 except existing Hub user IDs (24 lowercase hexadecimal Mongo ObjectId strings). UUIDs are opaque, **not monotonic**. Unknown request fields reject. Display plain text, never HTML/Markdown interpretation or external-link execution.
- Intake <=65,536 bytes; title trimmed once, 1..200 Unicode scalars and <=800 UTF-8 bytes; body normalize CRLF to LF and trim outer whitespace once, 1..4,000 scalars and <=16,384 bytes. Reject NUL and invalid UTF-8. Exact normalization repeated by server; confirmation displays normalized content. Canonical parent BSON <=1,048,576 bytes before insert.
- `selected` 1..500 unique user IDs; resolve at most 501 to detect overflow in **every** audience mode. Accept 1..500 resolved recipients, never truncate. selected IDs without grant are reported excluded; unknown IDs indistinguishable from ineligible. Admin audience = current `users.isAdmin == true` intersect `users.apps` containing `tabby-rush`; all = every current granted user; selected = requested IDs intersect grant. Admin sender must be current DB admin, but need not personally have receiver grant.
- JWT signature/expiry establishes identity only. Every admin route reads current DB sender role. Every receiver/device/stream route reads current DB user and grant; stream rechecks every 15s and before hints. Inbox/detail/read also check immutable membership. `notificationsAllowed` remains the existing email gate; it does not gate this feature. OS permission/capability is reported independently; no new preference or task-sync schema.
- Bearer header only; never access tokens in URLs, cookies substituted for bearer, redirects or app API-key bypass. Receiver routes are BEARER_ONLY, not strict-sync dual-auth. HTTPS on validated canonical origin; existing explicit debug loopback exception only. Responses `Cache-Control: no-store`; proxy buffering disabled for SSE.

## 2. Exact HTTP surface
Base `A=/api/v1/admin/apps/tabby-rush/announcements`, `U=/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/announcements`, `D=/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/notification-installs` (notation only; actual routes below). Existing notification preferences/email-test/legacy subscribe stay unchanged. Remove existing 501 `/api/v1/notifications/devices` POST and `/api/v1/notifications/devices/:token` DELETE; no compatibility aliases.

| Method and exact path | Authorization | Request | Success |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST `/api/v1/admin/apps/tabby-rush/announcements/audience-preview` | current DB admin | PreviewRequest | 200 AudiencePreview |
| POST `/api/v1/admin/apps/tabby-rush/announcements` | current DB admin | CreateRequest + `Idempotency-Key: UUIDv4` | 202 Acceptance, including replay |
| GET `/api/v1/admin/apps/tabby-rush/announcements` | current DB admin | `limit` default25/max50, optional `cursor` | 200 SentPage; all senders, senderId included |
| GET `/api/v1/admin/apps/tabby-rush/announcements/by-idempotency/{key}` | current DB admin; own senderId scope | key UUID | 200 Acceptance or 404 |
| GET `/api/v1/admin/apps/tabby-rush/announcements/{id}` | current DB admin | UUID | 200 SentDetail |
| GET `/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/announcements/inbox` | current user/grant | `limit` default25/max50, optional `cursor` | 200 InboxPage |
| GET `/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/announcements/unread` | current user/grant | none | 200 Unread |
| GET `/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/announcements/inbox/{id}` | current user/grant/member | UUID | 200 InboxItem |
| PUT `/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/announcements/inbox/{id}/read` | current user/grant/member | exactly `{}` | 200 ReadResult |
| GET `/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/announcements/stream` | current user/grant | optional Last-Event-ID, advisory only | 200 text/event-stream |
| PUT `/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/notification-installs/{installId}/binding` | current user/grant + install proof | BindRequest | 200 BindingResult |
| POST `/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/notification-installs/{installId}/unbind` | authenticated current owner + install proof; grant not required for cleanup | UnbindRequest | 200 BindingResult |
| GET `/api/v1/apps/tabby-rush/notification-installs/{installId}/binding` | authenticated user + install proof | none | 200 BindingStatus (no owner/token disclosure) |

Register static routes `by-idempotency`, `audience-preview`, `inbox`, `unread`, `stream` before UUID routes. Wrong app is not dynamically accepted. Unknown query fields, invalid UUID/cursor/limit ->400. Body limits on all routes: intake64KiB, preview32KiB, binding8KiB, read/unbind1KiB. GET has no body. TLS/proxy and configured rate limits return bounded sanitized errors.

### DTOs and examples
`AudienceSpec = {"mode":"selected","userIds":["507f1f77bcf86cd799439011"]}`; `all`/`admins` require absent userIds. PreviewRequest = `{ "audience": AudienceSpec }`.

```json
{
  "previewId":"a1c8249a-6f8d-4e73-97f5-dcebd10b407b",
  "appId":"tabby-rush",
  "audience":{"mode":"selected","userIds":["507f1f77bcf86cd799439011"]},
  "recipientIds":["507f1f77bcf86cd799439011"],
  "recipientCount":1,
  "excludedCount":0,
  "deliveryAvailability":{"inbox":"ready","desktopLive":"enabled","androidPush":"enabled"},
  "audienceDigest":"sha256:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
  "expiresAt":"2026-10-18T00:16:00.000Z"
}
```

AudiencePreview has exactly the example fields. `deliveryAvailability={inbox:"ready",desktopLive:"enabled"|"disabled",androidPush:"enabled"|"disabled"|"notConfigured"}` reports configured capability, never a device-delivery guarantee. UI renders it before confirmation. New intake requires enabled schema/read APIs, intake, durable worker and configured/enabled FCM; otherwise503, while idempotent replay and read/history remain available. Pausing provider sends after acceptance retains pending work until resume/expiry.

Preview IDs are opaque DB references bound to sender/app/audience/membership and expire after5min. Digest SHA-256 of canonical JSON sorted recipient IDs, appId and normalized audience; no signed-token key distribution. Display count and selected identities from existing admin directory, never infer delivered status. Send body:

```json
{
  "previewId":"a1c8249a-6f8d-4e73-97f5-dcebd10b407b",
  "audienceDigest":"sha256:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef",
  "title":"Maintenance notice",
  "body":"Please save your work before maintenance."
}
```

`Acceptance = {id,appId,senderId,createdAt,expiresAt,recipientCount,materializationState,dispatchSummary,replayed}`. `materializationState` pending|processing|retryable|complete|expired. `dispatchSummary={complete,fcm:{pending,processing,retryable,providerAccepted,failed,skipped,expired,ambiguousAttempts},sse:{pending,processing,hintPublished,failed,skipped,expired}}` counts durable targets, derived at query time; not acceptance prerequisite. Provider acceptance is never receipt. Until fanout complete, summary.complete=false; new targets can increase counts while materializing. Retryable renders as pending-with-retry in admin history. No synchronous send before acceptance.

`SentDetail = Acceptance + {title,body,audience,recipientIds,audienceDigest}`; `SentPage={items:[Acceptance + {title,audience}],nextCursor,serverNow}`. Admin history no device tokens or token-level provider responses.

`InboxItem={id,appId,title,body,createdAt,expiresAt,readAt}`; `readAt` null or canonical server timestamp. `InboxPage={items:[InboxItem],nextCursor,serverNow}`. `Unread={unreadCount,serverNow}`. `ReadResult={id,readAt,unreadCount,serverNow}`. All count/detail/list filters enforce parent active and membership; nonmember, missing and expired UUID all return404. Grant revoked ->403 `appAccessRevoked` and client clears all remote state.

Example inbox result (IDs and dates illustrative only):
```json
{"items":[{"id":"baf6dc3e-3099-4ae0-8767-985552ef0b82","appId":"tabby-rush","title":"Maintenance notice","body":"Please save your work before maintenance.","createdAt":"2026-10-18T00:12:00.000Z","expiresAt":"2027-01-16T00:12:00.000Z","readAt":null}],"nextCursor":null,"serverNow":"2026-10-18T00:12:02.000Z"}
```

All errors: `{ "error": {"code":"audienceChanged","message":"Recipient eligibility changed; preview again.","retryable":false,"requestId":"UUID","details":{}} }`. `details` only bounded safe fields (`field`, `limit`, `currentGeneration`, `retryAfterSeconds`), never content, credentials, tokens or another binding's owner. Error statuses:400 invalidRequest/invalidCursor;401 unauthenticated/tokenExpired;403 adminRequired/appAccessRevoked/installProofRejected;404 notFound/previewNotFound;409 audienceChanged/idempotencyConflict/staleInstallOperation/installOperationConflict/bindingChanged/tokenAlreadyBound;410 previewExpired/idempotencyExpired;413 requestTooLarge/audienceTooLarge;422 emptyAudience/invalidContent;429 rateLimited;503 announcementsDisabled/durableStorageUnavailable/providerNotConfigured. Retryability true only429/503; transport timeout has unknown commit outcome. Bad install proof and unknown binding GET use same403 to avoid an ownership oracle. Do not map announcement409 to task epoch/reset.

## 3. Preview confirmation and idempotent intake algorithm
1. Preview resolves full sorted deduplicated set from current users; enforce bound including selected input bound. Persist immutable preview with sender/app/spec/digest/recipientIds/createdAt/expiresAt using acknowledged write; preview is not dispatch intent.
2. Admin normalizes content, freezes `{previewId,audienceDigest,title,body}`, generates one UUID idempotency key **before** submit. Disable edits/submission while outcome unknown. Keep key+frozen body in current browser sessionStorage for bounded recovery, clear on logout; no access tokens stored there. Deadline90days; warn before exposing draft on shared browser, clear on owner mismatch.
3. Server first queries existing `(appId,senderId,key)` before inspecting current preview expiry/membership. Same canonical request digest returns202 original Acceptance (`replayed:true`), no re-resolution; conflicting body returns409. Digest canonical field-order JSON with normalized title/body and preview identity/digest (not mutable role data).
4. For genuinely new key, validate preview ownership/app/digest/expiry; resolve current same audience and compare full set/digest. Changed recipient identity or admin membership ->409 audienceChanged; do not silently replace preview. No zero-recipient success. DB eligibility can change immediately after check; this is validation-at-acceptance, not a Mongo transaction with user mutations. Dispatch/read always reauthorize current grant. Persist accepted immutable snapshot precisely as confirmed.
5. Under process broker admission lock reserve `acceptanceOrdinal` and current `acceptanceEpoch` (section7), then perform bounded parent insert with `w:1,j:true` on standalone or configured majority+j on replica set. Mongo write timeout5s; no fire-and-forget. Ordinal may be wasted; never reused. Return202 only after successful acknowledged journaled insert; unknown write outcome ->503 and instruct same-key recovery. Unique conflict rereads existing record/digest. No multi-document transactions.
6. Parent creationTime set once on insert; expiresAt=createdAt+90*24h. Key idempotency identity is retained in parent until this expiry; at/after expiry and before TTL return410 without content. After physical deletion, old-key dedup cannot be promised: clients MUST NOT reuse UUID keys or retry past original90day window. Fresh action always new key. No tombstone requirement for messages beyond retention; install tombstones are different.
7. Unknown submission: UI GET by-idempotency then retries exact POST/key if404, preserving original preview/body even if preview has since expired. Existing accepted record wins before preview validation. If truly uncommitted and preview expired/changed, show definitive rejection and require fresh preview+explicit confirmation+new key. Never generate a replacement message just because request timed out. Sender losing admin cannot recover history until restored; UI says permission lost, does not resend as another admin.
Canonical digest encoding is UTF-8 JSON without whitespace, fixed field order and ordinary JSON escaping: audience hash over `{appId,audience,recipientIds}`, normalized audience `{mode,userIds}` (userIds omitted unless selected, sorted/deduplicated); request hash over `{previewId,audienceDigest,title,body}`. SHA-256 lowercase hex prefixed `sha256:`. Do not hash UI labels, timestamps or mutable roles. Vectors freeze non-ASCII/escaping behavior.

## 4. Canonical Mongo storage and indexes
Collections separate from task sync. BSON dates server-side; field casing matches wire. All new writes journaled; failed index creation or unsupported durable write setting disables intake/worker (startup hard failure when feature enabled). Read primary. No raw secrets in documents.

| Collection | Immutable identity/content and mutable state | Required indexes |
|---|---|---|
