## Expanded deterministic gates
### G1 — audience, intake and browser journey (P02/P04; P12 browser proof)
1. Existing admin page permission controls remain present. Compose plain text, preview each selected/all/admin mode, show recipient count+normalized content, explicit confirm, pending state then honest history. Exercise empty/loading/error/page refresh and keyboard navigation.
2. Selected duplicates deduplicate; invalid IDs400; zero eligible422;501 eligible413 for every mode; no truncation. Title200 scalars/800bytes and body4000scalars/16KiB accepted within aggregate64KiB; invalid/one-over limits rejected. Parent BSON1MiB guard rejects before acknowledgement.
3. Change one recipient identity while keeping same count, revoke grant, change admin status, or join after preview. New send409 audienceChanged; accepted replay returns original snapshot; joining after acceptance never added. Grant revoked after validation cannot fetch/dispatch private content.
4. Same key same normalized body/preview digest202 replay; same key different body/preview409; different senders' same UUID keys independent; history by-key scoped sender. Unknown response/reload resolves one logical result without fresh confirm/key. Past retention410 while retained; no retry/reuse after original90day horizon or physical TTL deletion.
5. Admin role revoked with still-valid JWT ->403; another admin may view all sent history, cannot impersonate sender's by-key result. Plain text/XSS payload rendered literally, no external links, content never in URL/log.

### G2 — durability, leases, fanout and provider (P02/P03/P11; P12 process proof)
1. Record actual Mongo `hello`, journaling and configured `w/j` write/read-back; supported standalone test is required. Unsupported durability/index permission ->intake503/fail closed, not best-effort202. No transaction assumption.
2. Kill at each boundary: accepted parent before child; early read before materialization; recipient cutoff/target-batch persisted before dispatch upsert; partial deterministic children; all children before parent finish; parent finish with stale owner; dispatch send accepted before final update. After lease expiry reclaim processing parent **before** verifying/finishing, preserve first readAt and immutable bounded target batches; verify contiguous scan cursor chain and every child before completion.
3. Competing/overlapping workers, lease renew loss, expiredprocessing reclaim, stale fence finish, network timeout<lease, retries beyond expiry and attempt exhaustion. Verify bounds parent1/device4 concurrency and8 attempts; materialization storage retry retains pending authority while active.
4. Enumerate >50 bindings over multiple durable pages (e.g.121 fixture installs), without any per-user count cap or unbounded array. Kill between target-batch journal, child upserts and cursor advancement; recover frozen batches/idempotent jobs. Registration between acceptance and scan cutoff may be eligible; binds/rotations after cutoff do not backfill old push. Changed owner/generation/hash targets or revoked users skipped at send; inbox remains canonical. No-listener SSE finite skipped outcome, not retry loop.
5. Transport tests cover OAuth single-flight/cache/one401 refresh, wrong project/SENDER_ID_MISMATCH, token-specific vs generic400, UNREGISTERED,429 Retry-After>=60s,500/503 jitter and lost-response ambiguity. Live provider token/credential remains secret; history labels provider acceptance, not receipt.

### G3 — install fencing and account safety (P02/P05/P09/P10; P12 live)
1. First install UUID/proof insertion race: guessed ID/wrong proof403, no stealing. Server stores secret hash only, request owner derived from auth. Samegen/body replay idempotent; samegen/different body conflict; lower numeric generation stale; `"10"` newer than `"9"` numerically, not lexically.
2. Persist g before enqueue; crash before send then restart exact command; lost response repeats exact g/digest; current account switch reserves newer generation before any new operation. Test old g arriving before and after newer g+2; old may be transient prior server knowledge, can never overwrite accepted newer. GET status no other owner/token disclosure.
3. Old unbind expected g cannot delete new owner even if proposed operation number is larger. Token rotation and old invalid-token retirement match exact fence/hash. Token uniqueness across installs rejects conflict; lost Keystore creates new identity and fresh Firebase token instead of resetting server barrier. Tombstone not TTL-deleted.
4. Logout signed out/offline: no deletion-of-FCM-token prerequisite, unbind best effort, remote-only cleanup and callback fencing immediate. Local drain failure retains fenced runtime and blocks unsafe replacement. Late generic SDK alert is accepted; tapped UUID freshly reauthorized and wrong/no account shows safe inbox/login without later auto-opening in arbitrary account.

### G4 — shared inbox, SSE and retention (P02/P05/P06; P12 actual inbox)
1. Normal in-app entry plus native entry: list/detail/unread/pagination/read, compact/expanded/accessibility, empty/loading/error/revoked/offline. No fake task IDs or TodoAction. Offline hides body/detail, no durable content/read queue or Room schema change.
2. Cursor tampering/wrong scope/kind400; equal timestamps ordered by UUID lexical bytes; concurrent insert/read/expiry across pages no skip within stable upper-bound chain. Refresh resets chain; max200 cached items, hint buffer256 and dedup2048; cap overflow silently reconnects/reconciles instead of historical duplicate alert.
3. Race ready registration vs reserved acceptance vs baseline page fetch vs hint publication. Buffered new announcements may toast once desktop after authorization; pre-baseline/delayed>120s/old-epoch/recovered/replayed/disconnect-gap messages silent. No local wall-clock live classifier, UUID monotonicity assumption or Last-Event-ID durable replay claim.
4. Stream token expires, grant revoked, keepalive stops, parser oversized frame, network disconnect/lag/shutdown. Close/reopen with bounded backoff, current auth and generation; get all active parent-backed inbox even before materialization. Refresh visible read state/unread separately from creation pagination.
5. ServerNow+monotonic expiry anchor; exact90day API/read/render/send denial even with TTL lag. Reading never extends expiry. Orphan cleanup removes expired derived rows while preserving active parents and device generation tombstones. At next process start old in-memory content is absent, server inbox durable.

