<file path="plans/261017-0709-date-time-pickers/phase-01-picker-components.md">
# Phase 01 — Shared picker components and format utilities

## Overview
- Priority P2; status completed administratively on 2026-10-17 per request; effort 4h. Source sets DatePicker year range to `0..9999`; no supplied Gradle run validates this latest source change, and rendered boundary-year selection belongs to Phase 04.
- Use existing commonMain Material3 and kotlinx-datetime dependencies; no platform API imports or version upgrade.
- Read [master contract](plan.md), [Compose standards](../../docs/code-standards.md#3-kotlin-multiplatform--compose-guidelines), and current deadline validation before editing.

## Exclusive ownership
Create only:
- `shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/tabbyrush/shared/ui/date-time-pickers.kt`
- `shared/src/commonTest/kotlin/dev/tabbyrush/shared/ui/date-time-pickers-test.kt`
Read-only: `deadline-editor-section.kt`, `reminder-settings.kt`, `deadline-calculator-helpers.kt`, `todo-ui-state.kt`, build files, theme tokens.
No deletions. Phase 04 owns rendered-test wiring and semantics tests; do not modify those files.

## Key insights and design
- `DatePicker`, `DatePickerDialog`, `rememberDatePickerState`, `TimePicker`, and `rememberTimePickerState` belong to `androidx.compose.material3`; scope `ExperimentalMaterial3Api` opt-in here.
- Do not assume a Material3 `TimePickerDialog` exists at this pinned version. Use `AlertDialog` with `TimePicker` content, explicit Confirm/Cancel, and `onDismissRequest`.
- Use one shared button-style picker trigger rather than clickable editable text fields. Inline labels follow existing UI convention; no new icon dependency needed.
- Component state is tentative; only Confirm invokes value callback. Callers own domain updates and close visibility. Components never dispatch `TodoAction` or persist anything.

## Frozen component contract
```kotlin
@Composable internal fun DateTimePickerButton(
    label: String, value: String, onClick: () -> Unit,
    modifier: Modifier = Modifier, supportingText: String? = null
)
@Composable internal fun TabbyRushDatePickerDialog(
    initialDate: String, title: String,
    onConfirm: (String) -> Unit, onDismiss: () -> Unit
)
@Composable internal fun TabbyRushTimePickerDialog(
    initialTime: String, title: String,
    onConfirm: (String) -> Unit, onDismiss: () -> Unit,
    fallbackTime: String = "09:00"
)
```
- `DateTimePickerButton`: `OutlinedButton`, label and visible value (or “Choose date”/“Choose time” supplied as value); >=48dp minimum height, full click target, button role, no `EditableText`/`SetText`. Supporting text sits outside click semantics as appropriate.
- Trigger descriptions are caller-provided labels: `Deadline date`, `Deadline time`, `Date-only reminder anchor time`, `Default date-only anchor time`; expose current value through visible text/state description without duplicate spoken labels.
- Dialog headings identify field context; actions read `Confirm` and `Cancel`. Callers close on either callback; Confirm emits once, never additionally calls `onDismiss`.
- Date dialog uses `DatePicker` in calendar mode with `showModeToggle = false`; confirmation disabled when selection is null.
- Time dialog uses `rememberTimePickerState(is24Hour = true)` and renders `TimePicker(state = state)`; no `TimeInput`, keyboard-mode toggle, or seconds.
- Recreate picker state on each opening by conditionally composing dialog; cancellation must not leak tentative selection into reopening.

## Pure format utilities
Keep `internal object DateTimePickerFormats` in the component file; use these exact consumer-facing helpers:
```kotlin
fun dateToUtcMillisOrNull(value: String): Long?
fun utcMillisToDate(value: Long): String
fun parseTimeOrNull(value: String): kotlinx.datetime.LocalTime?
fun formatTime(hour: Int, minute: Int): String
```
- Date parsing accepts trimmed canonical four-digit `YYYY-MM-DD`, validates real calendar dates via `LocalDate`, returns null for empty/malformed/impossible values.
- Convert date to UTC day start; reverse via `Instant.fromEpochMilliseconds(value).toLocalDateTime(TimeZone.UTC).date`. Never use device/deadline timezone for selected milliseconds.
- DatePicker year range must match existing four-digit years (`0..9999`), not its default 1900–2100. Check pinned implementation supports boundary years; do not silently truncate or change an existing date.
- Invalid/empty initial date produces no selection; display current month only. Opening must not seed persisted date or enable Confirm without a selected day.
- Time parsing accepts only canonical 24-hour `HH:mm` after trimming; malformed input returns null. `formatTime` checks hour 0..23/minute 0..59 and pads both fields, with no locale-dependent formatting.
- Time dialog seeds from valid initial value; otherwise uses caller fallback (`09:00` anchors; `17:00` deadline). Fallback is tentative, never committed on opening/dismissal.
- No epoch instant/timezone conversion for wall-clock times, automatic DST adjustment, broad exception suppression, or normalization of persisted data.

## Implementation steps
1. Read pinned Material3 APIs and existing theme/layout patterns; choose only APIs available in Compose Multiplatform 1.7.3.
2. Implement/test pure parsing, canonical formatting, and UTC round-trip boundaries without adding a parallel domain validator.
3. Implement accessible trigger, calendar dialog, and clock dialog; keep helpers/components focused, using TabbyRush theme tokens and bounded scrollable content for small/large-font viewports.
4. Keep each new file under 200 lines; avoid a generic picker framework or extra state model. Do not refactor existing large consumer/test files.
5. Publish the signatures above and dismiss/confirm/seed rules as the Phase 01 handoff; only then release Phases 02 and 03 in parallel.

## Authored unit coverage
- Date round trips: leap day `2028-02-29`, year boundary `2026-12-31`, epoch `1970-01-01`, pre-epoch day, lower/upper supported four-digit years.
- UTC fixtures: selected UTC midnight returns the same date independently of caller/device timezone assumptions; exact epoch milliseconds asserted.
- Invalid dates: blank, malformed separator/padding, `2026-02-30`, non-leap `2025-02-29`, out-of-contract year width.
- Times: `00:00`, `09:05`, `12:00`, `23:59`; reject `24:00`, `09:60`, unpadded and seconds-bearing strings; formatter rejects invalid bounds.
- Keep tests pure here. Confirm/cancel/reopen and actual semantics are exercised through real composables in Phase 04, not simulated state copies.

## Success criteria and handoff
- Both dialogs and trigger implemented in commonMain; no new runtime dependency, typed-input fallback, or platform-specific implementation.
- Utilities produce canonical values; date selection cannot shift a day; valid pre-1900/post-2100 dates are not lost.
- Unit cases authored, shared API frozen, ownership respected. No build/test/lint/formatter execution in this phase; integration owner verifies after all implementation lands.
- Next: Phase 02 and Phase 03 consume contract without editing shared files.

## Risks and security
- Experimental API/date range differences: inspect pinned implementation before freezing API; escalate incompatibility to integration owner rather than add hidden restrictions.
- Nested dialogs/clock size: explicit labels, cancel path, bounded layout and Phase 04 actual focus/viewport checks.
- All state local and transient; no logs of user values, I/O, account access, alarm scheduling, or permission prompts.

## Unresolved questions
None requiring product input; pinned boundary-year behavior is an implementation compatibility gate, not permission to narrow supported data.
</file>

<file path="plans/261017-0709-date-time-pickers/phase-02-deadline-editor.md">
# Phase 02 — Deadline editor calendar and clock integration

## Overview
- Priority P2; status completed on 2026-10-17; effort 2h.
- Depends on completed [Phase 01](phase-01-picker-components.md) API handoff; runs in parallel with Phase 03.
- Replace all three date/time text fields in `DeadlineEditorSection`; retain all other behavior.
- Context: [master ownership](plan.md), [strict timezone rules](../../docs/code-standards.md#92-strict-timezone--dst-resolution).

## Exclusive ownership
Modify only:
- `shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/tabbyrush/shared/ui/deadline-editor-section.kt`
Read-only:
- `shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/tabbyrush/shared/ui/date-time-pickers.kt`
- `shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/tabbyrush/shared/ui/deadline-calculator-helpers.kt`
- `shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/tabbyrush/shared/ui/todo-editor.kt`
- `shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/tabbyrush/shared/contract/todo-ui-state.kt`
No created/deleted files. Do not edit shared components, settings, tests, build files, docs, or plan status.

## Key insights and invariants
- Current date, specific deadline time, and date-only anchor are `OutlinedTextField` inputs; timezone is a separate IANA field and remains editable.
- Existing state stores strings and dispatches `TodoAction.UpdateEditorState(editor.copy(...))`; preserve this boundary without controller/model changes.
- Existing date/time/anchor edits clear `chosenOffsetSeconds`. Preserve reset on actual value changes; opening/cancel/unchanged confirmation must not invalidate a user's DST overlap choice.
- Existing `DeadlineCalculatorHelpers` remains authoritative for invalid timezone, DST gaps/overlaps, reminder bounds, and schedule preview. Calendar validity does not imply a resolvable zoned instant.

## UI and action contract
| Existing value | Trigger label | Dialog/title | Confirm result |
|---|---|---|---|
| `editor.deadlineDate` | `Deadline date` | `TabbyRushDatePickerDialog`, same title | Copy date, clear chosen offset |
| `editor.deadlineTime` when `hasTime` | `Deadline time` | `TabbyRushTimePickerDialog`, same title; fallback `17:00` | Copy time, clear chosen offset |
| `editor.reminderAnchorTime` otherwise | `Date-only reminder anchor time` | `TabbyRushTimePickerDialog`, same title; fallback `09:00` | Copy anchor, clear chosen offset |
- Use Phase 01 `DateTimePickerButton`; show saved canonical value or explicit chooser prompt. Preserve date-only supporting text about reminder anchor and next-day overdue boundary.
- Trigger exposes click/button semantics and value, never an editable-text action or a typing hint.
- Confirm closes picker; emit exactly one update only when selected canonical value differs from current field. Use latest editor snapshot at callback time, preserving unrelated state.
- Cancel, outside-dismiss, Back/Escape where supported, and unchanged confirmation close picker without actions or offset resets.
- No text entry, `TimeInput`, calendar keyboard switch, automatic date/time assignment, or instant conversion in this file.

## Local state and composition
- Keep one nullable private picker target (`Date`, `DeadlineTime`, `AnchorTime`); one modal at most, keyed to editor identity/lifecycle.
- Dialog state exists only while target is visible. Closing and reopening reseeds from current editor, never the previous canceled selection.
- Close/dispose an open picker if its parent editor closes, task identity changes, deadline is disabled, or its time/anchor branch is no longer applicable. Do not allow a stale callback to update hidden fields.
- Do not make modal visibility part of `EditorState`, persist it, or reset task drafts as a side effect.

## Implementation steps
1. Import Phase 01 shared components and Compose local state; introduce the single active-target state inside this owned file.
2. Replace date text field in its existing date/timezone row with `DateTimePickerButton`, preserving weight and >=48dp target size. Keep IANA timezone input and its existing offset-reset callback.
3. Replace timed deadline field with clock trigger; replace date-only anchor field with clock trigger plus existing supporting copy.
4. Conditionally compose the corresponding shared dialog and wire confirm/dismiss actions per table, including no-op unchanged confirmation.
5. Preserve Set Deadline and Specific Time toggles, strict-v2 upgrade warning, overlap chips, reminder enable/lead/count/interval controls, validation text, and schedule preview.
6. Remove only newly obsolete date/time text-field labels/placeholders/imports; keep `OutlinedTextField` for timezone and numeric controls. Avoid unrelated layout/refactoring changes.
7. Report changed file and behavior review to integration owner; Phase 04 authors/runs tests after both parallel phases finish.

## Success criteria
- Deadline date is chosen from calendar; timed deadline and date-only anchor are chosen from clock; all three have accessible non-editable triggers.
- Confirmed date/time strings remain canonical; only the intended field and `chosenOffsetSeconds` change.
- Cancel/dismiss/reopen and unchanged confirmation preserve editor state and previous DST choice; invalid initial data is recoverable by selection without mutating it on open.
- Hiding deadline removes its pickers; `hasTime` controls which time trigger exists; no stale picker state crosses tasks.
- Explicit IANA timezone, DST gap rejection, overlap offset choice, strict-v2 save guard, and date-only overdue logic remain intact.
- No files outside exclusive ownership changed. No build/test/lint/formatter execution here.

## Verification scenarios for Phase 04
- Blank/new task: enable deadline, choose leap-day date, choose specific time, inspect emitted canonical update.
- Existing timed task: select different date/time and verify chosen offset clears; confirm same value and cancel modified tentative values without clearing it.
- Date-only task: change anchor through clock; validation still yields null deadline time and next-day overdue boundary.
- America/New_York: select `2026-03-08 02:30` and retain gap error; `2026-11-01 01:30` still requires explicit offset choice after changes.
- Toggle time/deadline, close editor, reopen another task; inspect visibility, current values, and no unintended action.

## Risks and security
- Parent dialog nesting and narrow date/timezone row may affect layout/focus; integration checks Android and desktop, large fonts, and keyboard traversal.
- Date/time edits must not schedule anything before existing save path; never introduce direct persistence, network, alarm, permission, or account operations.

## Next steps and unresolved questions
Hand off to Phase 04 only after Phase 03 also completes. No unresolved product questions.
</file>

