| AC11 | Complete/delete/clear/change rule/device-off/logout invalidate stale occurrence. Concurrent callback duplicates suppressed. Wipe admitted before post prevents any wiped-account title. Posted account-owned notifications removed where OS permits. Remote completion blocks old callbacks only after sync, not while unaware offline. | 06,07,08,09,11 | Deterministic interleaving regressions plus actual native cancellation/wipe and post-sync observation | **Automated Subset PASS / Native Removal Held (Gate G2)**: 1 test in `ReminderTeardownBarrierSqliteTest`, 7 in `AccountLeaveProtocolTest`, 4 in `ReminderDeliveryGateTest` PASS (stale occurrence invalidation, concurrent duplicate suppression, fail-closed teardown drain barrier); live OS notification center banner removal held pending Gate G2. |
| AC12 | At due+300000ms latest unconsumed due occurrence per task posts once; +300001 skips. Older due skip, future retain. Duplicate latest already consumed never falls back to older. Suspend/resume/forward-back clock changes/restart no catch-up burst. Durable-claim/post crash boundary may lose delivery; no exactly-once promise. | 07,08,09,11 | Controlled clock/shared vectors, actual resume/native late-callback state, documented crash-boundary behavior | **Automated Subset PASS / System Sleep Held (Gate G2)**: 9 tests in `ReminderScheduleCalculatorTest`, 6 in `DesktopReminderSchedulerTest`, 7 in `AdversarialSchedulerBoundaryTest` PASS (exact 300,000ms grace pass, 300,001ms skip, no backward jump burst, no older-opportunity resurrection); physical device sleep/wake and clock change timing held pending Gate G2. |

## Security and release cross-checks
- AC04 app-scoped admin and AC11 account wipe are release blockers. Legacy-receipt route scopes user/app and cannot mutate legacy task payloads.
- Manifest merged release receiver/permission/export/backup hardening; generic Android public lock-screen text and escaped Linux/Windows content.
- Normal dependency verification, target-isolated packages and artifact signing requirements; diagnostic verification-off/source scans insufficient for release.
- Existing-data protection includes drafts, uncertain successor FIFO and revisions, not only server task counts.
- No timing/exactly-once guarantee; no macOS/iOS, recurring tasks, snooze, FCM, desktop daemon/tray or arbitrary-schema feature.

## Evidence template
Each AC: status pending/pass/fail/blocked; target/OS/API/build/hash; contract/source migrationId; setup/input and expected state; actual command/action/output; sanitized screenshots/native timestamps; relevant before/after fingerprints; cleanup; limitations/blocker; responsible owner. Evidence belongs in existing `docs/` acceptance/evidence surfaces after execution; this matrix is not passing evidence.

## Unresolved questions
Windows/device/notification-service/operator access is required at execution. Missing prerequisite leaves its row blocked; no product scope question remains.
