# Release & Operations Acceptance

Document Version: 2.4.0  
Last Updated: 2026-10-21  
Status: **Release remains blocked. Native acceptance is not passed. Production migration is not authorized.**  
Related Docs: [Standard Sync Design](./standard-sync-cutover-design.md) · [Deployment Guide](./deployment-guide.md) · [Security & Recovery](./security-and-recovery.md) · [System Architecture](./system-architecture.md) · [Android Acceptance](./android-acceptance.md) · [Linux Acceptance](./linux-acceptance.md) · [Windows Acceptance](./windows-acceptance.md) · [Project Roadmap](./project-roadmap.md) · [Integrated Acceptance Evidence](../plans/261021-1552-tabbyrush-task-assignees/reports/04-integrated-acceptance-evidence.md)

---

## 1. Current Verdict

The current native client uses ordinary Glean Hub registration and standard sync. Strict-v1/v2/v3 is not the current binary protocol. Backend/API and standalone runtime evidence below is limited to disposable loopback/local services and does not approve a live migration or establish native UI/device acceptance.

**Do not state that TabbyRush native acceptance passed or that release is unblocked.** UI provider approval timed out twice and connected-device acceptance was not run. Production has not been migrated or authorized.

## 2. Current Evidence Matrix

| Area | Reported evidence | Acceptance boundary |
|---|---|---|
| Collaborative policy (G0) | Policy choices confirmed 2026-10-21: privacy-first purge of revoked remote payloads and unsent edits; whole-app capability cutoff (HTTP 426); single app-wide replica-set transaction guard (`_sync_assignment_fences`). | Confirmed by policy interview record (`06-validation-interview.md`); document-only, does not authorize production or approve release. |
| Collaborative runtime harnesses (G2, G3) | Dedicated harnesses delivered: `scripts/task-assignees-live-smoke.mjs` and `:desktopApp:runTaskAssigneesRuntimeSmoke`. Fail closed when disposable environment credentials are missing. | Prepared; NOT RUN during subagent phase per delegation rules (reserved for Main integration). |
| Standard Hub API/browser smoke | Disposable MongoDB 27191, Hub 3100, admin UI 3102. Ordinary provisioning, standard create/pull/delta/update/stale-conflict/delete, and unknown JSON retention passed. | Local/disposable only; no production migration or authorization. |
| Schema concurrency/UI | Nullable `customNotes` pasted in admin UI; `schemaVersion` 1→2, no-op remained 2, stale changed save returned 409 with draft preserved and latest schema read-only. | Admin/API behavior only; no generated native UI/Room fields. |
| Windows standalone native runtime | Strict Gradle JavaExec standalone main passed against disposable loopback services: Windows DPAPI, real HTTP auth, Room offline restart, two independent stores using actual coordinator push/pull/delta, schemaVersion 2, unknown nested JSON and nullable `customNotes` retained through native edit, parent/child sync and group deletion. | Runtime harness only; not an interactive Windows UI test, connected-Android proof, or cross-platform physical acceptance. |
| Offline Gradle/package suites | Parent reports current strict Gradle suites and Android/Desktop package outputs passed. | Build/test/package success does not establish native UI or device acceptance. Exact suite counts are maintained in parent verification reports. |
| Conversion operator | Parent reports 7/7 disposable-Mongo operator checks passed, including concurrency, deadline, and recovery. | Test evidence only. Operator does not authorize live production use. |
| Interactive native UI (G4, G5) | Provider interactive approval timed out during earlier cycles; collaborative Compose surfaces require interactive session. | Not run; native acceptance not passed. |
| Connected Android/device matrix (G4) | Connected-device acceptance was not run. | Not run; native acceptance not passed. |
| Production cutover (G7) | No production migration has occurred or been authorized. | Requires separate explicit approval and operator/backup/isolation gates. |
## 3. Current Release Criteria and Holds

A release decision requires, at minimum, review of current platform-specific acceptance documents, a successful interactive/native UI approval path, required connected-device verification, dependency/security review, and a separately authorized deployment decision. This document does not grant that authorization. Package creation and standalone harness execution are insufficient substitutes for connected-device or interactive acceptance.

Before any live standard-sync conversion, require separate explicit approval naming the exact Hub origin/database/app, backup/restore scope, external isolation plan, and maintenance window. The operator claim is durable and has no automatic expiry/takeover. After any failed mutating run, recover only through `maintenance.executionRecovery` with exact `expectedExecutionId`, `executorStopped: true` plus `executorStopEvidence`, `mongoOperationsDrained: true` plus `mongoDrainEvidence`, and `authorizedActions` containing `recoverExecution`. Renew and verify the maintenance window before each collection rename and registry CAS. See [Deployment Guide](./deployment-guide.md) and [Security & Recovery](./security-and-recovery.md). A live cutover still requires its own approval.

## 4. Historical Strict-v3 Acceptance Snapshot

**Historical record, 2026-10-20 and earlier; superseded for current protocol and not a release decision.** Earlier Phase 06/strict-v3 material described parent/child and deadline features, strict schema fingerprints/receipts, strict-v2/v3 upgrade tooling, and Gates G1–G7. One earlier Cycle 2 QA report claimed 749 verification targets across 15 groups, including one ignored live-Mongo test and Gradle execution with dependency verification disabled. Those counts and strict gate statuses describe that historical run only; they do not represent current standard-sync test counts, current native UI/device acceptance, or production readiness.

Former strict-v2 and strict-v3 runbooks have been retired; strict-specific scripts named by historical material have been removed. Consult [Project Roadmap](./project-roadmap.md) for current planning status; this release document intentionally does not duplicate roadmap tracking.
</file>

<file path="scripts/build-windows-remote-msi.ps1">
<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Builds the native C++/WinRT x64 toast DLL, packages the Compose desktop distributable,
    and produces an identity-verified per-user MSI with System.AppUserModel.ID shortcut property.

.DESCRIPTION
    Phase 08 Windows Native Packaging Script.
    Validates MSVC C++20, JDK 21, and WiX 3 toolchains.
    Compiles desktopApp/native/windows/tabbyrush-toast.dll, packages the desktop application,
    harvests file components with WiX heat, compiles with candle, and links with light.

.PARAMETER SkipNativeBuild
    Skips C++ DLL compilation if pre-built Release DLL already exists.

.PARAMETER RunNativeTests
    Executes native ctest suite after building DLL.
#>

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [switch]$SkipNativeBuild,
    [switch]$RunNativeTests,
    [string]$Verification = "off",
    [string]$Version = ""
)

Set-StrictMode -Version Latest
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"

$repoRoot = Resolve-Path (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot "..")
Write-Host "=== TabbyRush Windows MSI Packaging Pipeline ===" -ForegroundColor Cyan
Write-Host "Repository root: $repoRoot"

# 1. Toolchain Verification
Write-Host "`n1. Verifying Toolchains..." -ForegroundColor Cyan

$cmakeCmd = Get-Command cmake -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
if (-not $cmakeCmd) {
    throw "CMake not found in PATH. Install CMake 3.20+ and configure MSVC x64 build tools."
}
Write-Host "[PASS] CMake found: $($cmakeCmd.Source)" -ForegroundColor Green

$candleCmd = Get-Command candle -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
$lightCmd = Get-Command light -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
$heatCmd = Get-Command heat -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
if (-not ($candleCmd -and $lightCmd -and $heatCmd)) {
    $wixCandidates = @(
        "C:\Program Files (x86)\WiX Toolset v3.14\bin",
        "C:\Program Files (x86)\WiX Toolset v3.11\bin",
        "C:\ProgramData\chocolatey\bin",
        "C:\ProgramData\chocolatey\lib\wixtoolset\tools"
    )
    foreach ($cand in $wixCandidates) {
        if (Test-Path "$cand\candle.exe") {
            $env:PATH = "$cand;$env:PATH"
            $candleCmd = Get-Command candle -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
            $lightCmd = Get-Command light -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
            $heatCmd = Get-Command heat -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
            if ($candleCmd -and $lightCmd -and $heatCmd) { break }
        }
    }
}
if (-not ($candleCmd -and $lightCmd -and $heatCmd)) {
    throw "WiX Toolset v3 (heat.exe, candle.exe, light.exe) not found in PATH or standard candidate directories. Install WiX Toolset 3.11+."
}
Write-Host "[PASS] WiX Toolset found: $($candleCmd.Source)" -ForegroundColor Green

$javaCmd = Get-Command java -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
if (-not $javaCmd) {
    throw "Java runtime not found in PATH. JDK 21 is required."
}
Write-Host "[PASS] Java runtime found: $($javaCmd.Source)" -ForegroundColor Green

# 2. Native C++/WinRT DLL Build
$nativeSourceDir = Join-Path $repoRoot "desktopApp\native\windows"
$nativeBuildDir = Join-Path $repoRoot "desktopApp\build\native\windows"
$nativeDllPath = Join-Path $nativeBuildDir "Release\tabbyrush-toast.dll"

if (-not $SkipNativeBuild) {
    Write-Host "`n2. Building native C++/WinRT x64 DLL..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
    if (-not (Test-Path $nativeBuildDir)) {
        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $nativeBuildDir -Force | Out-Null
    }

    & cmake -S $nativeSourceDir -B $nativeBuildDir -A x64
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "CMake configuration failed for tabbyrush-toast" }

    & cmake --build $nativeBuildDir --config Release
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "CMake build failed for tabbyrush-toast Release" }

    if ($RunNativeTests) {
        Write-Host "`n   Running native ctest suite..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
        & ctest --test-dir $nativeBuildDir -C Release --output-on-failure
        if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Native ctest suite failed" }
    }
}

if (-not (Test-Path $nativeDllPath)) {
    throw "tabbyrush-toast.dll not found at expected path: $nativeDllPath"
}

$dllHash = (Get-FileHash -Path $nativeDllPath -Algorithm SHA256).Hash
Write-Host "[PASS] tabbyrush-toast.dll built successfully. SHA-256: $dllHash" -ForegroundColor Green

# Stage DLL into desktopApp resources for JNA classpath fallback
$resourceTargetDir = Join-Path $repoRoot "desktopApp\src\windowsMain\resources\win32-x86-64"
if (-not (Test-Path $resourceTargetDir)) {
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $resourceTargetDir -Force | Out-Null
}
Copy-Item $nativeDllPath (Join-Path $resourceTargetDir "tabbyrush-toast.dll") -Force
Write-Host "[PASS] tabbyrush-toast.dll staged into resources: $resourceTargetDir" -ForegroundColor Green

# 3. Build Compose Desktop Distributable
Write-Host "`n3. Building Compose Desktop application distributable..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
$gradlew = Join-Path $repoRoot "gradlew.bat"
$propMatch = Get-Content (Join-Path $repoRoot "gradle.properties") | Select-String "^appVersion\s*=\s*(.*)$"
$appVer = if ($Version) { $Version } elseif ($propMatch) { $propMatch.Matches.Groups[1].Value.Trim() } else { "1.0.0" }
Write-Host "Target package version: $appVer" -ForegroundColor Cyan
& $gradlew :desktopApp:createDistributable "-PdesktopTarget=windows" "-PappVersion=$appVer" "--dependency-verification=$Verification"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Gradle :desktopApp:createDistributable failed" }

$distDir = Join-Path $repoRoot "desktopApp\build\compose\binaries\main\app\TabbyRush"
if (-not (Test-Path $distDir)) {
    throw "Application distributable bundle not found at: $distDir"
}

# Copy native DLL and icon into distributable bundle root and app subfolder
Copy-Item $nativeDllPath (Join-Path $distDir "tabbyrush-toast.dll") -Force
$appSubdir = Join-Path $distDir "app"
if (Test-Path $appSubdir) {
    Copy-Item $nativeDllPath (Join-Path $appSubdir "tabbyrush-toast.dll") -Force
}

$iconSrc = Join-Path $repoRoot "desktopApp\src\windowsMain\resources\tabbyrush.ico"
if (Test-Path $iconSrc) {
    Copy-Item $iconSrc (Join-Path $distDir "TabbyRush.ico") -Force
}
# Ensure app.runtime is configured in TabbyRush.cfg so jpackage launcher locates the bundled JVM runtime,
# and ensure both TabbyRush.cfg and .env are strictly BOM-free UTF-8 for jpackage launcher compatibility.
$utf8NoBom = New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)
$cfgFile = Join-Path $appSubdir "TabbyRush.cfg"
if (Test-Path $cfgFile) {
    $rawCfgBytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($cfgFile)
    $hasCfgBom = ($rawCfgBytes.Length -ge 3 -and $rawCfgBytes[0] -eq 0xEF -and $rawCfgBytes[1] -eq 0xBB -and $rawCfgBytes[2] -eq 0xBF)
    if ($hasCfgBom) {
        $cfgText = $utf8NoBom.GetString($rawCfgBytes, 3, $rawCfgBytes.Length - 3)
    } else {
        $cfgText = $utf8NoBom.GetString($rawCfgBytes, 0, $rawCfgBytes.Length)
    }
    $cfgLines = $cfgText -split "\r?\n"
    $needsRuntime = -not ($cfgLines -match "^app\.runtime=")
    if ($needsRuntime -or $hasCfgBom) {
        $newCfg = @()
        foreach ($line in $cfgLines) {
            $newCfg += $line
            if ($needsRuntime -and $line.Trim() -eq "[Application]") {
                $newCfg += "app.runtime=`$APPDIR\..\runtime"
            }
        }
        [System.IO.File]::WriteAllLines($cfgFile, $newCfg, $utf8NoBom)
        Write-Host "[PASS] Normalized TabbyRush.cfg (BOM-free UTF-8, app.runtime verified)" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Host "[PASS] TabbyRush.cfg already contains app.runtime and is BOM-free" -ForegroundColor Green
    }
}

$distEnv = Join-Path $distDir ".env"
if (-not (Test-Path $distEnv)) {
    $defaultEnv = "APPROVED_HUB_ORIGIN=https://api-glean-hub.qm-hub-v001.cloud`nTABBYRUSH_API_KEY=XoaJSoximq8EhK06IjXAQCOqKqRtM6qy`n"
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($distEnv, $defaultEnv, $utf8NoBom)
    Write-Host "[PASS] Generated default .env (BOM-free UTF-8)" -ForegroundColor Green
} else {
    $rawEnvBytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($distEnv)
    if ($rawEnvBytes.Length -ge 3 -and $rawEnvBytes[0] -eq 0xEF -and $rawEnvBytes[1] -eq 0xBB -and $rawEnvBytes[2] -eq 0xBF) {
        $cleanEnvText = $utf8NoBom.GetString($rawEnvBytes, 3, $rawEnvBytes.Length - 3)
        [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($distEnv, $cleanEnvText, $utf8NoBom)
        Write-Host "[PASS] Normalized existing .env (BOM stripped, custom values preserved)" -ForegroundColor Green
    }
}

Write-Host "[PASS] Application distributable bundled with native DLL, icon, runtime config, and default env" -ForegroundColor Green
# 4. WiX Harvesting and MSI Packaging
Write-Host "`n4. Packaging per-user MSI with WiX..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
$wixWorkDir = Join-Path $repoRoot "desktopApp\build\windows-installer"
if (-not (Test-Path $wixWorkDir)) {
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $wixWorkDir -Force | Out-Null
}

$harvestedWxs = Join-Path $wixWorkDir "application-files.wxs"
$installerWxs = Join-Path $repoRoot "desktopApp\packaging\windows\installer.wxs"
$outputMsiDir = Join-Path $repoRoot "desktopApp\build\compose\binaries\main\msi"
if (-not (Test-Path $outputMsiDir)) {
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $outputMsiDir -Force | Out-Null
}
$outputMsi = Join-Path $outputMsiDir "TabbyRush-$appVer.msi"

# WiX Heat: harvest distributable folder
& heat dir "$distDir" -cg AppFiles -dr INSTALLDIR -scom -sreg -srd -var var.SourceDir -gg -out "$harvestedWxs"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "WiX heat harvesting failed" }

# WiX Candle: compile WXS sources
& candle -arch x64 "-dSourceDir=$distDir" "-dProductVersion=$appVer" -out "$wixWorkDir\" "$installerWxs" "$harvestedWxs"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "WiX candle compilation failed" }

# WiX Light: link MSI (suppress ICE validation with -sval for per-user harvested files)
$installerWixObj = Join-Path $wixWorkDir "installer.wixobj"
$appFilesWixObj = Join-Path $wixWorkDir "application-files.wixobj"
& light -ext WixUIExtension -sval -out "$outputMsi" "$installerWixObj" "$appFilesWixObj"
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "WiX light linking failed" }

if (-not (Test-Path $outputMsi)) {
    throw "MSI package was not generated at expected path: $outputMsi"
}

$msiHash = (Get-FileHash -Path $outputMsi -Algorithm SHA256).Hash
Write-Host "`n=== Packaging Complete ===" -ForegroundColor Green
Write-Host "MSI Artifact: $outputMsi" -ForegroundColor Green
Write-Host "SHA-256: $msiHash" -ForegroundColor Green

# 5. Verification via windows-package-smoke.ps1
$smokeScript = Join-Path $repoRoot "scripts\windows-package-smoke.ps1"
if (Test-Path $smokeScript) {
    Write-Host "`n5. Executing package smoke test..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
    & $smokeScript -DistDir $distDir -MsiPath $outputMsi -ExpectedVersion $appVer
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "windows-package-smoke.ps1 audit failed" }
}

Write-Host "`n[SUCCESS] Windows Remote MSI Packaging and Audit Successful!" -ForegroundColor Green
</file>

<file path="scripts/windows-package-smoke.ps1">
<#
.SYNOPSIS
    TabbyRush Windows Desktop & MSI Package Verification Smoke Runner.
    Phase 10 Validation & Diagnostics Harness.

.DESCRIPTION
    Verifies the Windows build environment, inspects self-contained distributable bundles,
    audits packaged JARs for target isolation (Windows DPAPI present, Linux D-Bus absent),
    computes SHA-256 hashes, inspects Authenticode signatures, and validates MSI metadata.

.PARAMETER Diagnose
    Displays host OS, Java runtime, jpackage, and WiX toolset status.

.PARAMETER DistDir
    Path to the createDistributable output directory to validate.

.PARAMETER MsiPath
    Path to the packaged .msi file to inspect.

.EXAMPLE
    .\scripts\windows-package-smoke.ps1 -Diagnose
    .\scripts\windows-package-smoke.ps1 -DistDir desktopApp\build\compose\binaries\main\app\TabbyRush
    .\scripts\windows-package-smoke.ps1 -MsiPath desktopApp\build\compose\binaries\main\msi\TabbyRush-1.0.0.msi
#>

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [switch]$Diagnose,
    [string]$DistDir = "",
    [string]$MsiPath = "",
    [string]$ExpectedVersion = ""
)

Set-StrictMode -Version Latest
$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"

function Show-Diagnostics {
    Write-Host "=== TabbyRush Windows Desktop Environment Diagnostics ===" -ForegroundColor Cyan

    # 1. Host OS
    $os = [System.Environment]::OSVersion
    $arch = [System.Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable("PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE")
    Write-Host "1. Host OS: Windows $($os.Version) ($arch)"

    # 2. Java Runtime
    Write-Host -NoNewline "2. Java Runtime: "
    $javaCmd = Get-Command java -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    if ($javaCmd) {
        $prev = $ErrorActionPreference
        $ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"
        $javaVer = (& java -version 2>&1 | Select-Object -First 1).ToString()
        $ErrorActionPreference = $prev
        Write-Host "PRESENT ($javaVer) at $($javaCmd.Source)" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Host "NOT FOUND in PATH" -ForegroundColor Red
    }

    # 3. jpackage tool
    Write-Host -NoNewline "3. jpackage tool: "
    $jpCmd = Get-Command jpackage -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    if ($jpCmd) {
        $jpVer = & jpackage --version 2>&1 | Select-Object -First 1
        Write-Host "PRESENT ($jpVer) at $($jpCmd.Source)" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Host "NOT FOUND in PATH" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    }

    # 4. WiX Toolset (candle.exe, light.exe)
    Write-Host -NoNewline "4. WiX Toolset (candle / light): "
    $candleCmd = Get-Command candle -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    $lightCmd = Get-Command light -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    if ($candleCmd -and $lightCmd) {
        Write-Host "PRESENT (candle: $($candleCmd.Source), light: $($lightCmd.Source))" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Host "NOT INSTALLED in PATH (Required for :desktopApp:packageMsi; install WiX 3.11+)" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    }

    # 5. PowerShell Environment
    Write-Host "5. PowerShell Version: $($PSVersionTable.PSVersion)"
    Write-Host "6. Execution Policy: $(Get-ExecutionPolicy)"

    Write-Host "=== Diagnostics Complete ===" -ForegroundColor Cyan
}

function Test-DistributableBundle {
    param([string]$Path)

    Write-Host "`n=== Auditing Distributable Directory: $Path ===" -ForegroundColor Cyan

    if (-not (Test-Path $Path)) {
        Write-Error "Distributable directory does not exist: $Path"
        return $false
    }

    # 1. Verify launcher executable
    $exeCandidates = @(
        (Join-Path $Path "TabbyRush.exe"),
        (Join-Path $Path "tabbyrush.exe")
    )
    $launcher = $exeCandidates | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ } | Select-Object -First 1

    if ($launcher) {
        $fileInfo = Get-Item $launcher
        Write-Host "[PASS] Launcher executable found: $($fileInfo.Name) ($([math]::Round($fileInfo.Length / 1KB, 2)) KB)" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] Launcher executable (TabbyRush.exe) not found in $Path"
        return $false
    }

    # 2. Verify bundled runtime
    $jvmCandidates = @(
        (Join-Path $Path "runtime\bin\server\jvm.dll"),
        (Join-Path $Path "runtime\bin\java.dll"),
        (Join-Path $Path "runtime\bin\java.exe")
    )
    $runtimeBin = $jvmCandidates | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ } | Select-Object -First 1
    if ($runtimeBin) {
        Write-Host "[PASS] Bundled Java runtime found: $runtimeBin" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Host "[WARN] Bundled runtime not found at standard path in $Path\runtime" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    }

    # 2b. Verify native C++/WinRT toast DLL
    $dllCandidates = @(
        (Join-Path $Path "tabbyrush-toast.dll"),
        (Join-Path $Path "app\tabbyrush-toast.dll")
    )
    $nativeDll = $dllCandidates | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ } | Select-Object -First 1
    if ($nativeDll) {
        $dllInfo = Get-Item $nativeDll
        Write-Host "[PASS] Native C++/WinRT toast DLL found: $($dllInfo.FullName) ($([math]::Round($dllInfo.Length / 1KB, 2)) KB)" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] Native C++/WinRT toast DLL (tabbyrush-toast.dll) NOT found in $Path"
        return $false
    }
    # 2.5 Verify launcher config has app.runtime for bundled JVM and is strictly BOM-free
    $cfgCandidates = @(
        (Join-Path $Path "app\TabbyRush.cfg"),
        (Join-Path $Path "TabbyRush.cfg")
    )
    $cfgFile = $cfgCandidates | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ } | Select-Object -First 1
    if ($cfgFile) {
        $rawCfgBytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($cfgFile)
        if ($rawCfgBytes.Length -ge 3 -and $rawCfgBytes[0] -eq 0xEF -and $rawCfgBytes[1] -eq 0xBB -and $rawCfgBytes[2] -eq 0xBF) {
            Write-Error "[FAIL] Launcher configuration file ($cfgFile) contains UTF-8 BOM (0xEF 0xBB 0xBF). Native jpackage launcher fails with 'Fail to launch JVM'!"
            return $false
        }
        Write-Host "[PASS] Launcher configuration is BOM-free (no UTF-8 BOM detected): $cfgFile" -ForegroundColor Green

        $cfgContent = Get-Content -Path $cfgFile
        if ($cfgContent -match "^app\.runtime=") {
            Write-Host "[PASS] Launcher configuration defines explicit app.runtime: $cfgFile" -ForegroundColor Green
        } else {
            Write-Host "[NOTE] Launcher configuration omits explicit app.runtime (jpackage defaults to adjacent bundled runtime)" -ForegroundColor Yellow
        }
    } else {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] Launcher configuration file (TabbyRush.cfg) NOT found in $Path"
        return $false
    }

    # 2.6 Verify all present .env files are BOM-free
    $envCandidates = @(
        (Join-Path $Path ".env"),
        (Join-Path $Path "app\.env")
    )
    foreach ($envFile in $envCandidates) {
        if (Test-Path $envFile) {
            $rawEnvBytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($envFile)
            if ($rawEnvBytes.Length -ge 3 -and $rawEnvBytes[0] -eq 0xEF -and $rawEnvBytes[1] -eq 0xBB -and $rawEnvBytes[2] -eq 0xBF) {
                Write-Error "[FAIL] Distributable .env ($envFile) contains UTF-8 BOM (0xEF 0xBB 0xBF). Distributable configuration files must follow the BOM-free packaging standard."
                return $false
            }
            Write-Host "[PASS] Distributable .env is BOM-free (no UTF-8 BOM detected): $envFile" -ForegroundColor Green
        }
    }
    # 3. Verify packaged application JARs and inspect classes
    $appDir = Join-Path $Path "app"
    if (-not (Test-Path $appDir)) {
        $appDir = $Path
    }

    $jarFiles = @(Get-ChildItem -Path $appDir -Filter "*.jar" -Recurse -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)
    if ($jarFiles.Count -eq 0) {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] No JAR files found in app directory: $appDir"
        return $false
    }

    Write-Host "[INFO] Found $($jarFiles.Count) packaged JAR artifact(s) in $appDir"

    Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem

    $foundWindowsVault = $false
    $foundWindowsSpi = $false
    $foundLinuxDbus = $false
    $registeredProviders = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()

    foreach ($jar in $jarFiles) {
        if ($jar.Name -like "*dbus*" -or $jar.Name -like "*secret-service*") {
            $foundLinuxDbus = $true
        }
        $zip = $null
        try {
            $zip = [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::OpenRead($jar.FullName)
            foreach ($entry in $zip.Entries) {
                if ($entry.FullName -like "*WindowsDpapiVault*") {
                    $foundWindowsVault = $true
                }
                if ($entry.FullName -eq "META-INF/services/dev.tabbyrush.desktop.CredentialVaultProvider") {
                    $stream = $entry.Open()
                    $reader = $null
                    try {
                        $reader = New-Object System.IO.StreamReader($stream)
                        while (-not $reader.EndOfStream) {
                            $line = $reader.ReadLine().Trim()
                            if ($line -ne "" -and -not $line.StartsWith("#")) {
                                $registeredProviders.Add($line)
                                if ($line -eq "dev.tabbyrush.desktop.windows.WindowsDpapiVaultProvider") {
                                    $foundWindowsSpi = $true
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    } finally {
                        if ($null -ne $reader) { $reader.Close() }
                        $stream.Close()
                    }
                }
                if ($entry.FullName -like "*LinuxSecretServiceVault*" -or $entry.FullName -like "*org/freedesktop/dbus/*") {
                    $foundLinuxDbus = $true
                }
            }
        } catch {
            Write-Error "[FAIL] Corrupted or unreadable JAR file detected: $($jar.FullName): $($_.Exception.Message)"
            return $false
        } finally {
            if ($null -ne $zip) {
                $zip.Dispose()
            }
        }
    }

    if ($foundWindowsVault) {
        Write-Host "[PASS] WindowsDpapiVault class packaged in desktop bundle" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] WindowsDpapiVault class NOT found in packaged JARs"
        return $false
    }

    if ($foundWindowsSpi) {
        Write-Host "[PASS] WindowsDpapiVaultProvider registered in META-INF/services" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] WindowsDpapiVaultProvider SPI registration NOT found in packaged JARs"
        return $false
    }

    if ($registeredProviders.Count -ne 1) {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] Expected exactly one CredentialVaultProvider, but found $($registeredProviders.Count): $($registeredProviders -join ', ')"
        return $false
    } else {
        Write-Host "[PASS] Exactly one CredentialVaultProvider registered: $($registeredProviders[0])" -ForegroundColor Green
    }

    if (-not $foundLinuxDbus) {
        Write-Host "[PASS] Target Isolation: Zero Linux D-Bus / SecretService classes leaked into Windows bundle" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] Target Isolation Violated: Linux D-Bus classes detected in Windows bundle"
        return $false
    }

    Write-Host "=== Distributable Audit Passed ===" -ForegroundColor Green
    return $true
}

function Test-MsiPackage {
    param([string]$Path)

    Write-Host "`n=== Auditing Windows Installer Package: $Path ===" -ForegroundColor Cyan

    if (-not (Test-Path $Path)) {
        Write-Error "MSI file does not exist: $Path"
        return $false
    }

    $fileItem = Get-Item $Path
    Write-Host "1. File: $($fileItem.Name) ($([math]::Round($fileItem.Length / 1MB, 2)) MB)"

    # Compute SHA-256
    $hash = Get-FileHash -Path $Path -Algorithm SHA256
    Write-Host "2. SHA-256 Digest: $($hash.Hash)"

    # Check Authenticode signature
    $sig = Get-AuthenticodeSignature -FilePath $Path
    Write-Host "3. Authenticode Status: $($sig.Status) ($($sig.StatusMessage))"
    if ($sig.Status -eq "NotSigned") {
        Write-Host "   [NOTE] Package is unsigned (development/testing build; no public publisher certificate)" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    }

    # Inspect MSI properties via Windows Installer COM
    $installer = $null
    $database = $null
    $view = $null
    try {
        $installer = New-Object -ComObject WindowsInstaller.Installer
        $database = $installer.GetType().InvokeMember(
            "OpenDatabase",
            [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod,
            $null,
            $installer,
            @($Path, 0)
        )
        $view = $database.GetType().InvokeMember(
            "OpenView",
            [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod,
            $null,
            $database,
            @("SELECT Property, Value FROM Property")
        )
        $view.GetType().InvokeMember("Execute", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod, $null, $view, $null)

        $targetProps = @("ProductName", "ProductVersion", "ProductCode", "UpgradeCode", "Manufacturer")
        $extractedProps = @{}
        Write-Host "4. MSI Metadata Properties:"
        while ($true) {
            $record = $view.GetType().InvokeMember("Fetch", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod, $null, $view, $null)
            if ($null -eq $record) { break }
            $prop = $record.GetType().InvokeMember("StringData", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::GetProperty, $null, $record, @(1))
            $val = $record.GetType().InvokeMember("StringData", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::GetProperty, $null, $record, @(2))
            if ($targetProps -contains $prop) {
                Write-Host "   - ${prop}: ${val}"
                $extractedProps[$prop] = $val
            }
        }
        try { $view.GetType().InvokeMember("Close", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod, $null, $view, $null) } catch {}
        # Validate mandatory properties and expected values
        if ($extractedProps["ProductName"] -ne "TabbyRush") {
            Write-Error "[FAIL] ProductName mismatch: expected 'TabbyRush', got '$($extractedProps['ProductName'])'"
            return $false
        }
        if (-not [string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($ExpectedVersion)) {
            $expectedProductVersion = $ExpectedVersion
        } else {
            $repoRoot = Resolve-Path (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot "..")
            $gradleProps = Join-Path $repoRoot "gradle.properties"
            if (Test-Path $gradleProps) {
                $propMatch = Get-Content -Path $gradleProps | Select-String "^appVersion=\s*(.+)$"
                if ($propMatch) { $expectedProductVersion = $propMatch.Matches[0].Groups[1].Value.Trim() }
                else { $expectedProductVersion = "1.0.0" }
            } else {
                $expectedProductVersion = "1.0.0"
            }
        }
        if ($extractedProps["ProductVersion"] -ne $expectedProductVersion) {
            Write-Error "[FAIL] ProductVersion mismatch: expected '$expectedProductVersion', got '$($extractedProps['ProductVersion'])'"
            return $false
        }
        if ($extractedProps["Manufacturer"] -ne "TabbyRush Team") {
            Write-Error "[FAIL] Manufacturer mismatch: expected 'TabbyRush Team', got '$($extractedProps['Manufacturer'])'"
            return $false
        }
        if ($extractedProps["UpgradeCode"] -ne "{A6C507C8-88FE-4E49-8F43-A6125039281A}") {
            Write-Error "[FAIL] UpgradeCode mismatch: expected '{A6C507C8-88FE-4E49-8F43-A6125039281A}', got '$($extractedProps['UpgradeCode'])'"
            return $false
        }
        if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($extractedProps["ProductCode"])) {
            Write-Error "[FAIL] ProductCode is missing or empty"
            return $false
        }
        Write-Host "[PASS] All mandatory MSI metadata properties validated successfully" -ForegroundColor Green

        # 5. Verify AUMID in MsiShortcutProperty table
        $shortcutView = $null
        try {
            try {
                $shortcutView = $database.GetType().InvokeMember(
                    "OpenView",
                    [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod,
                    $null,
                    $database,
                    @("SELECT PropertyKey, PropVariantValue FROM MsiShortcutProperty")
                )
            } catch {
                $shortcutView = $database.GetType().InvokeMember(
                    "OpenView",
                    [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod,
                    $null,
                    $database,
                    @("SELECT PropertyKey, PropVariant_ FROM MsiShortcutProperty")
                )
            }
            $shortcutView.GetType().InvokeMember("Execute", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod, $null, $shortcutView, $null)
            $foundAumid = $false
            while ($true) {
                $rec = $shortcutView.GetType().InvokeMember("Fetch", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod, $null, $shortcutView, $null)
                if ($null -eq $rec) { break }
                $key = $rec.GetType().InvokeMember("StringData", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::GetProperty, $null, $rec, @(1))
                $val = $rec.GetType().InvokeMember("StringData", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::GetProperty, $null, $rec, @(2))
                if ($key -eq "System.AppUserModel.ID") {
                    if ($val -eq "dev.tabbyrush.desktop") {
                        $foundAumid = $true
                        Write-Host "[PASS] MsiShortcutProperty System.AppUserModel.ID is correctly set to 'dev.tabbyrush.desktop'" -ForegroundColor Green
                    } else {
                        Write-Error "[FAIL] MsiShortcutProperty System.AppUserModel.ID mismatch: expected 'dev.tabbyrush.desktop', got '$val'"
                        return $false
                    }
                }
            }
            if (-not $foundAumid) {
                Write-Error "[FAIL] MsiShortcutProperty System.AppUserModel.ID NOT found in MSI"
                return $false
            }
        } catch {
            Write-Error "[FAIL] MsiShortcutProperty table query failed: $($_.Exception.Message)"
            return $false
        } finally {
            if ($null -ne $shortcutView) {
                try { $shortcutView.GetType().InvokeMember("Close", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod, $null, $shortcutView, $null) } catch {}
            }
        }
    } catch {
        Write-Error "[FAIL] MSI COM inspection failed: $($_.Exception.Message)"
        return $false
    } finally {
        if ($null -ne $view) {
            try { $view.GetType().InvokeMember("Close", [System.Reflection.BindingFlags]::InvokeMethod, $null, $view, $null) } catch {}
        }
        if ($null -ne $database) {
            [System.Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::ReleaseComObject($database) | Out-Null
        }
        if ($null -ne $installer) {
            [System.Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::ReleaseComObject($installer) | Out-Null
        }
    }

    Write-Host "=== MSI Audit Complete ===" -ForegroundColor Green
    return $true
}

# Entrypoint routing
if ($Diagnose) {
    Show-Diagnostics
    exit 0
}

$success = $true

if ($DistDir -ne "") {
    $res = Test-DistributableBundle -Path $DistDir
    if (-not $res) { $success = $false }
}

if ($MsiPath -ne "") {
    $res = Test-MsiPackage -Path $MsiPath
    if (-not $res) { $success = $false }
}

if (-not $Diagnose -and $DistDir -eq "" -and $MsiPath -eq "") {
    Write-Host "No action specified. Run with -Diagnose, -DistDir <path>, or -MsiPath <path>." -ForegroundColor Yellow
    Show-Diagnostics
}

if ($success) { exit 0 } else { exit 1 }
</file>

